{
  "name": "vector_light_shader_only",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "The custom shader on its own, with every other \u00a727 composition switched off, on a midnight room with a one-cell GAP in the east wall and one torch. Three arms and nothing else: vanilla, the shader with its subtraction OFF -- which computes max(0, ours - 0), i.e. MoteGlow's output exactly, and so shows what SHAPE the fragment program can draw at all -- and the shader composing max(0, ours - vanilla) over an untouched vanilla flood. No mask, no suppression, no flat beam, no per-cell max: the point is to see the shader's own output rather than a composition of four things. vector_light_shader_max_available is pinned in both shader arms because standing down is by design silent and --mod-overlay does not carry asset bundles.",
